WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.334
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome.

00:00:02.334 --> 00:00:04.437
Welcome to
"The Tonight Show."

00:00:04.437 --> 00:00:05.672
Thank you very much.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:07.507
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.507 --> 00:00:08.607
I don't know about you guys,

00:00:08.607 --> 00:00:11.143
but I am stuffed
with wings and nachos

00:00:11.143 --> 00:00:14.313
from my impeachment
trial party, and --

00:00:14.313 --> 00:00:16.683
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.118
Yeah, of course,
the big story today

00:00:18.118 --> 00:00:20.286 line:0%
is that Trump's second
impeachment trial

00:00:20.286 --> 00:00:22.354 line:0%
has finally begun.

00:00:22.354 --> 00:00:24.424 line:0%
That's right, two
impeachments are historic,

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.659
but just like Tom Brady,
Trump won't rest

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.127
until he gets to seven.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:30.496
[ Laughter ]

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:32.165
That's right.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:34.500
Seriously, I can't believe
we're talking about Trump again.

00:00:34.500 --> 00:00:37.169
Even herpes knows when
to take a break once in a while.

00:00:37.169 --> 00:00:38.571
I mean, just --

00:00:38.571 --> 00:00:40.907
But tonight,
everybody's talking about

00:00:40.907 --> 00:00:43.810
one of Trump's lawyers,
Bruce Castor.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:46.746
He kicked off Trump's defense

00:00:46.746 --> 00:00:48.581
and never really
got to the point.

00:00:48.581 --> 00:00:49.849
But this is real.

00:00:49.849 --> 00:00:51.450
Check this guy out.

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.185 line:0%
-My name is Bruce Castor.

00:00:53.185 --> 00:00:56.522 line:0%
When I was growing up
in suburban Philadelphia...

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.725 line:0%
Here's little Bruce --
8, 9, 10 years old --

00:00:58.725 --> 00:01:00.993 line:0%
listening to this
back in the late '60s.

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:03.229 line:0%
We still know
what records are, right?

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:05.898 line:0%
On the thing you put the needle
down on, and you play it.

00:01:05.898 --> 00:01:07.834 line:0%
You ever heard
Everett Dirksen's voice,

00:01:07.834 --> 00:01:12.405 line:0%
it's the most commanding,
gravelly voice.

00:01:12.405 --> 00:01:15.675 line:0%
"Gallant Men"
is the name of the --

00:01:15.675 --> 00:01:17.843 line:0%
of the, uh...

00:01:17.843 --> 00:01:19.645 line:0%
of the album.

00:01:19.645 --> 00:01:22.048
-[ Groans ]
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:22.048 --> 00:01:24.717
[ Laughter ]

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.553
Even Joe Biden was like,
"Come on, man.

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:28.654
Wrap it up."

00:01:28.654 --> 00:01:30.622
If the Senate had
an orchestra pit,

00:01:30.622 --> 00:01:31.924
they'd be playing
him off like...

00:01:31.924 --> 00:01:35.294
♪ Neh-deh-la-dah-dee-dee-dee ♪

00:01:35.294 --> 00:01:36.529
"Get on out of here."

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.097
Oh, gosh.
Given who his boss is,

00:01:38.097 --> 00:01:39.198
I'm pretty sure that that was

00:01:39.198 --> 00:01:41.867
his opening
and closing statement.

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:43.169
[ Imitates Trump ]
"You're fired."

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:44.804
[ Normal voice ]
Meanwhile, Rudy Giuliani

00:01:44.804 --> 00:01:47.273
was watching like,
"Damn, this guy's good."

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.175
[ Laughter ]

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:51.143
Yep, he started talking
this afternoon

00:01:51.143 --> 00:01:52.478
and should be done around

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:55.748
the fourth hour
of the "Today" show tomorrow.

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:58.585 line:0%
Man, could that guy possibly
waste any more of our time?

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:01.988 line:0%
[ Bottle crinkles ]

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:04.357 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.791 --> 00:02:06.959
[ Imitates bottle crinkling ]

00:02:06.959 --> 00:02:08.561
A little crinkle crunch.

00:02:08.561 --> 00:02:10.296
He -- [ Laughs ]

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:12.198
He crunched it out a little bit.

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:13.399
Alex, can we play that
one more time

00:02:13.399 --> 00:02:16.302 line:0%
just so I can hear
that water bottle crinkle?

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.870 line:0%
[ Bottle crinkles softly ]

00:02:17.870 --> 00:02:18.972 line:0%
[ Bottle crinkles loudly ]

00:02:18.972 --> 00:02:21.807 line:0%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.807 --> 00:02:22.908
He's having fun, man.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:24.376
Come on.

00:02:24.376 --> 00:02:25.677
Well, guys, I think
it's safe to say,

00:02:25.677 --> 00:02:27.213
no one wants to
relive the events

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:28.814
of last month's insurrection,

00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:31.751
but it has led
to some interesting flubs.

00:02:31.751 --> 00:02:33.253
Here, I'll show you what I mean.
Listen to this.

00:02:33.253 --> 00:02:37.390 line:0%
-Donald John Trump
incited the erection --

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:38.825 line:0%
insurrection.

00:02:38.825 --> 00:02:40.726 line:0%
-Does the President of the
United States believe

00:02:40.726 --> 00:02:43.228 line:0%
that former president Trump
incited an erect--

00:02:43.228 --> 00:02:45.398 line:0%
excuse me, incited
an insurrection?

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:47.367 line:0%
-Who has been impeached for
inciting the erection.

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.335 line:0%
-He did incite an erection
on the Capitol.

00:02:49.335 --> 00:02:51.971 line:0%
-If I have to embrace someone
who just incited an erectio--

00:02:51.971 --> 00:02:53.206 line:0%
an insurrection--

00:02:53.206 --> 00:02:55.608
[ Laughing ]
Oh, my.

00:02:55.608 --> 00:02:57.343
-Hey.
-Wow.

00:02:57.343 --> 00:02:58.911
[ Chuckles ]
-Wow.

00:02:58.911 --> 00:03:00.179
[ Drumsticks tapping ]

00:03:00.179 --> 00:03:04.650
-Well, President Biden and
Vice President Harris

00:03:04.650 --> 00:03:07.419
met with the CEOs
of Lowe's, The Gap,

00:03:07.419 --> 00:03:09.054
Walmart, and JPMorgan

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:11.390
to discuss
the President's stimulus plan.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:13.559
There was an awkward moment
when the CEO of Walmart

00:03:13.559 --> 00:03:15.561
walked up to Biden and said,
"Hey, I know you.

00:03:15.561 --> 00:03:17.096
You're one of our greeters."

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:19.465
[ Laughter ]

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:23.236
They would have invited
the CEO of Old Navy,

00:03:23.236 --> 00:03:24.837
but they were afraid
it would lead to Biden

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.639
telling another long story.

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:29.876
[ Imitating Biden ]
"The Old Navy used to be
called The Boat Squad.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:32.545
[ Laughter ]

00:03:34.046 --> 00:03:36.449
It was led by Dicky Kimblewad.

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:37.483
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.483 --> 00:03:39.752
He had one arm
and three nipples."

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:41.854
[ Laughter ]

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:43.389
[ Normal voice ]
Well, last night,
there was another episode

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.992
of "The Bachelor,"
and things got pretty intense.

00:03:45.992 --> 00:03:47.126
And the emotions on that show

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:48.461
can be a little hard
to handle sometimes,

00:03:48.461 --> 00:03:49.595
so we thought we could help.

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.297
Here's a clip from the episode,

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.967
but re-voiced with the least
emotional person we know --

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:55.101
Siri.

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.370
This is "Let's Get Siri-ous."

00:03:57.370 --> 00:03:58.704
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:58.704 --> 00:04:00.606
Man: [ Whispers ]
<i> Let's get Siri-ous.</i>

00:04:00.606 --> 00:04:02.141
-Weak bitches lie.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.643
-You know what
a weak bitch does?

00:04:03.643 --> 00:04:05.578
They tear down other people
to make themselves look better.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:07.212
That's what you did.

00:04:07.212 --> 00:04:08.881
Hold on.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.382
I need to fluff my hair.

00:04:10.382 --> 00:04:12.618
I forgot who I am for a second.

00:04:12.618 --> 00:04:17.556 line:0%
♪♪

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:19.691
I had a weak-bitch moment,
but I'm back.

00:04:19.691 --> 00:04:21.561
[ Laughter, applause ]

00:04:21.561 --> 00:04:22.795
-Wow.

00:04:22.795 --> 00:04:25.231
[ Laughing ]

00:04:26.431 --> 00:04:28.934
Oh, she came back.
Oh, my gosh.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.338
Hey, get this --
a pair of Nike sneakers

00:04:32.338 --> 00:04:34.140
designed for
former president Obama

00:04:34.140 --> 00:04:37.242
are going on sale for $25,000.

00:04:37.242 --> 00:04:39.011
Huh.

00:04:39.011 --> 00:04:41.213
No offense, but those look like
the perfect complement

00:04:41.213 --> 00:04:42.415
to Obama's dad jeans.

00:04:42.415 --> 00:04:43.616
I'm just saying.

00:04:45.217 --> 00:04:46.886
If the Obama sneakers
are too expensive,

00:04:46.886 --> 00:04:49.422
for 50 bucks, you can buy
a pair of SKECHERS Shape-Ups

00:04:49.422 --> 00:04:52.525
designed for Joe Biden,
so it's up to you.

00:04:52.525 --> 00:04:54.393
I had no idea
Nike did this for presidents.

00:04:54.393 --> 00:04:56.295
Apparently, they made
the same sneaker for Trump

00:04:56.295 --> 00:04:58.097
but with a built-in
ankle monitor.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:04:59.098
It's pretty cool.

00:04:59.098 --> 00:05:01.000
[ Audience groans ]

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.769
Interesting to see.
It's just --

00:05:02.769 --> 00:05:04.903
[ Applause ]

00:05:04.903 --> 00:05:06.238
Well, this is going viral.

00:05:06.238 --> 00:05:09.875
Down in Texas, a judge was
holding a virtual hearing,

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.244
and one of the lawyers
had some trouble

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:13.512
with a Zoom filter.

00:05:13.512 --> 00:05:14.947
This is real.

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:16.148
Check this out.

00:05:16.148 --> 00:05:19.651
-John, I believe
you have a filter turned on

00:05:19.651 --> 00:05:22.021
in the video settings.

00:05:22.021 --> 00:05:24.657
-Yes, and I don't know
how to remove it.

00:05:24.657 --> 00:05:27.426
One of our assistants
was just trying to...

00:05:27.426 --> 00:05:29.895
I'm here live.
I'm not a cat.

00:05:29.895 --> 00:05:30.930
-[ Laughs ] Aw.

00:05:30.930 --> 00:05:32.231
What?

00:05:32.231 --> 00:05:33.900
[ Laughter ]

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.302
What?

00:05:36.302 --> 00:05:38.004
I'm glad he cleared that up.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:40.573
"I am not a cat, okay?"

00:05:40.573 --> 00:05:42.241
The courtroom
sketch artist was like,

00:05:42.241 --> 00:05:43.876
"Ugh, didn't think I'd be
drawing whiskers today,

00:05:43.876 --> 00:05:45.444
but, hey, what can you do?"

00:05:45.444 --> 00:05:46.879
Yeah, when he saw that,
Trump was like...

00:05:46.879 --> 00:05:49.815
[ Imitates Trump ]
"I want that guy."

00:05:49.815 --> 00:05:51.283
[ Normal voice ]
It got weird when
the filter disappeared

00:05:51.283 --> 00:05:52.885
and the lawyer
was licking himself.

00:05:52.885 --> 00:05:54.754
[ Laughter ]

00:05:56.922 --> 00:05:58.391
Get this --
a company has created

00:05:58.391 --> 00:06:01.393
a new laptop prototype
with seven screens.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:02.862
Take a look at this thing.

00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:05.397
I can't wait to be on a plane

00:06:05.397 --> 00:06:07.533
when some guy in the
middle seat opens that up.

00:06:07.533 --> 00:06:09.869
[ Laughs ] "You mind
if I use the armrests, dude?

00:06:09.869 --> 00:06:12.738
[ Grunts ]
Check all my screens there.

00:06:12.738 --> 00:06:14.573
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.573 --> 00:06:17.476
Gotta make sure
my Grindr's up.

00:06:17.476 --> 00:06:19.845
The Twitter is on the --

00:06:19.845 --> 00:06:21.381
Gotta make sure that..."

00:06:22.481 --> 00:06:23.682
You're not that
important, buddy.

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:25.351
It's all good.

00:06:25.351 --> 00:06:28.221
And, finally, after dashing
across the Australian freeway

00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:30.322
and causing a multi-car pile-up,

00:06:30.322 --> 00:06:33.525
a koala got comfortable
in the car of its rescuer.

00:06:33.525 --> 00:06:34.894
Look at this guy.

00:06:34.894 --> 00:06:36.595
Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:06:36.595 --> 00:06:37.963
-Wow.
-See?

00:06:37.963 --> 00:06:40.298
When your country beats COVID,
that is your top story.

00:06:40.298 --> 00:06:41.600
You know what I'm saying?

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:43.202
That's what we got
to look forward -- We got that.

00:06:43.202 --> 00:06:45.071
We have a great show
for you tonight, everybody.

